    "speaker": "Emiel",
    "seconds": 60,
    "notes": "A pretrained human forecasting model teaches a robot policy through intermediate-feature distillation. The CALVIN ABC-to-D setting tests an unseen scene after robot-policy training on A/B/C. Average success rises from 65.9 to 67.5 percent, a 1.6 percentage point gain; average task-chain length rises from 3.29 to 3.38. Single-task success is lower than AR-VRM: 0.859 versus 0.901. This is not direct zero-shot control of a physical robot by human hand poses.",
