  {
    "index": 15,
    "title": "What the evidence supports",
    "speaker": "Emiel",
    "seconds": 75,
    "notes": "Strength: Exo is training-only, both module families have ablation support, and evaluation spans three benchmarks plus robot transfer. Limits: automatic labels and filtered easy-visible cases can bias the benchmark; reimplementations and no reported run variance limit comparison confidence; MPJPE is root-aligned so it does not establish global reaching accuracy; language necessity is not isolated; 802 GFLOPs baseline means low extra overhead does not establish real-time operation. State these as our analysis.",
